WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.000
You might have seen Salvation Mountain
in music videos or in documentaries.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.620
It attracts people.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.660
Even for folks who aren't religious,
this hill,

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.254
covered in half a million
gallons of latex paint

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.220
and sitting in the middle
of the sun blasted California desert,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.555
this hill has something about it.

00:00:15.555 --> 00:00:17.982
And it was the work of just one person.

00:00:17.982 --> 00:00:20.489
Leonard Knight was a man
who, he was kinda lost,

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:22.500
just cruising around trying
to figure out what to do.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.888
He discovered Jesus,
so he had a mission,

00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:26.092
and then he started doing things.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.959
and he made a hot air balloon,
like 200 foot,

00:00:28.959 --> 00:00:31.606
sewed it all together with all
these praises to God on it.

00:00:31.606 --> 00:00:33.045
Brought it out here.

00:00:33.045 --> 00:00:35.617
The desert ended up taking
its toll on the balloon,

00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:37.312
but he stayed and he built this mountain.

00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:39.707
But you really have to look at it
to get the big picture.

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:43.109
That sand hill, that way,
shows exactly what was here.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.680
Couple little straggly bushes
and a flat hill of sand.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.900
And Leonard built all this.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.920
He added extra clay, hay bales,
whatever it took to build this all up.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.440
He just kept goin' and goin'.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:53.928
He was going to dome the whole thing off.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.640
And he never really thought
of himself as a artist,

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.360
he more thought of himself as
somebody just doing what he was doing.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.640
He was a persistent dude.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.000
This mountain originally fell
after three and a half years of building.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.679
He rebuilt.

00:01:04.679 --> 00:01:07.245
He had a passion, and
this is so beautiful.

00:01:07.245 --> 00:01:09.056
28 years of dedication.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.760
Try dedicating 28 minutes
to something nowadays, realistically.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.160
I think about that.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.620
Leonard Knight had no training,
no collective of other folks around him.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.760
The technical term is outsider art.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.334
He wasn't inspired by anyone else's work,

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.939
unless you count God.

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:25.669
He wasn't imitating great artists,

00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:27.817
he wasn't asking for feedback
from friends around him,

00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:31.927
he just created this, and
it resonated with the world.

00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:33.785
Years after his death,
there's a group of people here

00:01:33.785 --> 00:01:36.397
who give their time preserving his legacy.

00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:38.556
We have so many people
coming from everywhere.

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:41.379
I've met people from
little countries in Africa,

00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:44.665
to all over Europe, to
floating little islands

00:01:44.665 --> 00:01:46.410
and this and that, it's amazing.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.580
And some people, they come here
for the religional deals on it, cool.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:54.260
Some people come here for pretty people
takin' pretty pictures at a pretty place,

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:57.266
which-- be respectful, and that's cool too.

00:01:57.266 --> 00:01:58.641
It's getting you out, you're doing stuff.

00:01:58.641 --> 00:02:02.180
They're getting off their couches
and getting away from the TVs and stuff,

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.780
which is... TV is awesome too,
though, so I'm not knocking TV.

00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:06.722
Paint donations that we get here,

00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:08.045
most of them come from the visitors.

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:09.740
They'll bring a couple of cans,

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.900
couple of cans turn into a hundred cans.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.688
Let's say I wanted to paint that heart.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:15.592
I would have to wait a
considerable amount of time

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.060
'til I had enough really beautiful red
to mix up to paint that heart.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.780
And then it makes it
so much more satisfying

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.080
when you do do it.
But the best thing is,

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.540
that our paint comes really
from the heart, from the people.

00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:26.946
Even if this were to fall apart,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:30.620
it's inspired so many people,
filmmakers, pilgrims, and tourists alike,

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.460
that it'll live on in memories,
in photographs, and yes, in music videos.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.700
The moment I knew about it,

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.613
I wanted to come here
and see it for myself.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.480
I started volunteering here because

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.620
I realised how important it was
to everybody that came here.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.073
And so I volunteered more,

00:02:46.073 --> 00:02:48.166
and eventually they had me
be like a greeter

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:49.698
and I would, "Da-de-dah-de-dah."

00:02:49.698 --> 00:02:51.417
Then I was like,
"Well, can I paint while I greet?"

00:02:51.417 --> 00:02:52.531
"Oh yeah, go ahead."

00:02:52.531 --> 00:02:53.646
"Da-de-dah-de-dah."

00:02:53.646 --> 00:02:54.911
Next thing you know I'm the caretaker

00:02:54.911 --> 00:02:56.304
and I've been living
here a year and a half.

00:02:56.304 --> 00:02:58.928
In my heart I'm the
preservationist of this place.

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:02.040
I've tried to paint it all the same
and make it beautiful and keep it.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.758
When I fix it, I fix it good.

00:03:03.758 --> 00:03:06.313
If I can't fix it good,
don't fix it yet, leave it alone.

00:03:06.313 --> 00:03:07.671
Leave it alone 'til you can do it right.

00:03:07.671 --> 00:03:09.877
The biggest thing is: this is about love.

00:03:09.877 --> 00:03:12.814
Leonard's love was God,
and his relationship with Jesus.

00:03:12.814 --> 00:03:14.788
But all kinds of love is awesome.

00:03:14.788 --> 00:03:18.180
Like these people all just love cruising around
and hanging out, doing stuff.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.860
That's all makes everything better.

00:03:19.861 --> 00:03:22.462
We don't think about all
the dumb crap in this world.

00:03:22.462 --> 00:03:24.300
And you know what?
Then the dumb crap in this world

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.277
really becomes dumb crap in this world

00:03:26.277 --> 00:03:27.902
and it doesn't have a powerful voice.

00:03:27.902 --> 00:03:31.385
There's not many places in
this world where it's good,

00:03:31.385 --> 00:03:32.906
and nothing's expected of you.

00:03:32.906 --> 00:03:34.230
We hope you would donate money to us

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.080
'cause that's how we do it,
but if you don't, cool!

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.380
We got free souvenirs anyway,
and there's constantly stuff going on.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.340
But if you show up on a Saturday,
you'll get to see what this is really about.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.456
It is just packed with
people having a good time,

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.020
respecting the mountain,
respecting each other, it's awesome!

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.319
Some folks would say
it's divine inspiration.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.960
Some folks would be a bit more cynical
and say that it had to be someone.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.333
Of all the millions,
perhaps billions of people

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.640
who ever tried creating art
with no experience and no training,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.277
yes, statistically someone
was going hit the jackpot.

00:04:02.277 --> 00:04:05.992
But it's difficult to be cynical here.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.480
So I brought a couple of cans of paint along
as part of my own pilgrimage,

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.379
because as it turns out,

00:04:11.379 --> 00:04:14.296
I want to help preserve this as well.

